  "rules": [
    "When recent history shows a strong downtrend (e.g., Example 1), the model systematically overestimates future prices by ignoring immediate mean reversion; apply a downward correction of 5-8% to the forecasted path.",
    "The model exhibits significant lag in reacting to sentiment spikes (sentiment=1.0); when positive sentiment appears, the true outcome often reverses direction or crashes immediately rather than rising as predicted.",
    "In volatile regimes with mixed sentiment history, the model fails to capture high-frequency volatility and assumes a smooth linear trend; reduce forecasted variance by 30% and flatten the slope.",
    "When the last 5 days show a price spike followed by neutral/negative sentiment, the model's continued upward trajectory is invalid; apply an immediate downward correction equal to the distance between the peak and the recent low.",
    "The model consistently underestimates downside risk during periods of high volatility (Examples 3-5); increase the lower bound of the forecast range by 10% relative to the mean."
  ]
}
